ite","checks":"write","code_quality":"write","contents":"write","copilot_requests":"write","deployments":"write","discussions":"write","drives":"write","issues":"write","merge_queues":"write","metadata":"read","models":"read","packages":"write","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","repository_projects":"write","security_events":"write","statuses":"write","vulnerability_alerts":"read"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6122999355","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/pull/57#issuecomment-6122999355","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/57","id":6122999355,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSN6Nm88AAAABbPWOOw","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-12T11:05:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T11:05:00Z","body":"## AI Security Review\n**Experiment condition:** C\n**Automated operational score:** 70/100 — CRITICAL — APPROVE_WITH_COMMENTS\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **CRITICAL · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · Unrestricted inbound RDP (TCP/3389) permitted from any internet source**\n  - Category rationale: The Terraform code directly configures an inbound Allow rule for TCP/3389 from source 0.0.0.0/0 at priority 301, which is evaluated before the DenyAllInbound rule at priority 4096. This permits unrestricted internet-originating RDP traffic to any destination in the associated subnet, constituting a concrete and demonstrated security weakness regardless of the stated testing intent. The tfsec scanner independently identifies the same rule under AVD-AZU-0048 and AVD-AZU-0047. Policy SEC-001 requires explicit justification for any publicly exposed resource; the in-code comment references TC03 but no supplied policy document approves this exposure.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_network_security_group.nsg, security_rule 'AllowRDP': direction='Inbound', access='Allow', protocol='Tcp', destination_port_range='3389', source_address_prefix='0.0.0.0/0', priority=301. DenyAllInbound is at priority=4096, which is evaluated after 301. tfsec findings AVD-AZU-0048 and AVD-AZU-0047 on the same resource corroborate.\n  - Analysis: The NSG rule 'AllowRDP' in azurerm_network_security_group.nsg allows inbound TCP traffic on port 3389 from source_address_prefix 0.0.0.0/0 (all internet addresses) at priority 301. Because priority 301 is evaluated before the DenyAllInbound rule at priority 4096, this rule is fully effective. Any host on the public internet can initiate RDP sessions to resources attached to this NSG. The inline comment labels this 'deliberately unrestricted RDP access for controlled security testing only (TC03)', but this annotation does not restrict actual network access and no supplied policy document grants an exemption for public RDP exposure.\n  - Impact: Unrestricted RDP exposure is a well-known attack surface for brute-force credential attacks, exploitation of RDP protocol vulnerabilities (e.g., BlueKeep-class), and lateral movement. Even in a research/testing context, any resource successfully deployed behind this NSG is exposed to the internet. If a VM or other RDP-capable resource is later attached to this subnet, it will be immediately reachable from the entire internet without further configuration change.\n  - Recommendation: Restrict source_address_prefix to a known, controlled IP range (e.g., a specific operator IP or corporate egress CIDR) rather than 0.0.0.0/0. If broad access is required for testing, document the approved source ranges and apply a time-bound or conditionally applied rule. If public RDP exposure is truly required under SEC-001, obtain and record explicit written approval referencing the resource and scope, and supply that evidence in the PR. Consider using Azure Bastion or a jump host with JIT access as a lower-risk alternative for remote access scenarios.\n\n### Policy mappings\n- **SEC-001** — No resource should be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified. (finding F-001)\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6122999355/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15